// Copy to Local.xcconfig (gitignored) for a stable code signature.
//
// Cleared signs ad-hoc by default so anyone can clone and build without an
// Apple account. The cost is that every rebuild produces a new app identity,
// which invalidates the Keychain entry holding your token — you have to
// reconnect after each build.
//
// Setting a real identity makes the signature stable and the token stick.
// List yours with:  security find-identity -v -p codesigning
// The team is the OU field of that certificate.
//
// CLEARED_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development: Your Name (XXXXXXXXXX)
// CLEARED_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID

// ── Mac App Store ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The AppStore configuration (what Product → Archive builds) is sandboxed and
// can be signed under a different team from your day-to-day builds — the one
// that holds your Apple Distribution certificate. Without these it falls back
// to ad-hoc signing, which still builds and runs but cannot be uploaded.
//
// CLEARED_APPSTORE_TEAM = YOURTEAMID
// CLEARED_APPSTORE_IDENTITY = Apple Development
